	'k16150b86' => 'Mentors',
	'k16a804e3' => 'The best way to evaluate our training environment is to attend an open morning. Our next open morning takes place on Saturday 21 November at 10:00. Open mornings are completely free to attend, and there is no need to make an advance booking.',
	'k16f10c3b' => 'I had stepped away from care work for eleven years to raise my family, and the equipment had changed completely, explains Camille Roux. Camille enrolled in our six-week Return to Care course to refresh her skills. The program allowed her to practice modern electric hoists, review slide-sheet protocols, and learn updated infection control standards.',
	'k17420354' => 'Host a student',
	'k17e16467' => 'Placement is supervised practice, not cover for a short-staffed floor. You join one of our twenty-two partner homes with a named mentor, and only once you have shown in the practice room that you can transfer, wash and talk with someone safely.',
	'k186bfe84' => 'Eight units, assessed in the practice room and on placement.',
	'k18b85817' => 'Choosing the right course depends on your availability and goals. The Core Care Certificate requires thirty-two full-time weeks and 420 placement hours at $6,800. The Evening Route covers the identical syllabus over forty-eight weeks for $7,200. Return to Care provides a six-week refresher for $1,150 without external placement.',
	'k18e6581d' => 'Six weeks part-time for people who have cared before and want to move and handle with confidence again.',
	'k19863570' => 'Open morning: Saturday 21 November at 10:00',
