	'k3fa0a427' => 'from an office desk, retail counter, or trade brings valuable life experience to care. You do not need previous medical background to begin; we teach every transfer, record-keeping method, and bedside routine from first principles with steady repetition in our practice room.',
	'k4083138d' => 'Camille Roux',
	'k410bdc80' => 'Unit 5 examines equality, diversity, and person-centred care. Unit 6 covers health, safety, and moving and handling. Unit 7 provides comprehensive instruction on infection prevention and control. Unit 8 explores dementia awareness and cognitive support. Each unit integrates classroom instruction with practical skills drills.',
	'k412a6b97' => 'You will participate in basic ergonomics and communication exercises. This practical session gives you a realistic experience of our training methods while allowing our faculty to assess your empathy, listening ability, physical coordination, and suitability for the demands of residential care.',
	'k41ae564c' => 'Next open morning',
	'k4281849e' => 'After eight years behind a bank counter, I wanted work where my attention went directly to people rather than transactions, recalls Noor Haddad. Noor enrolled in the Core Care Certificate seeking a meaningful change of daily work. The transition into practical training was intense, particularly mastering safe moving techniques in the practice room.',
