	'k611063e8' => 'Rosa Delgado',
	'k6214e95b' => 'Our campus at 18 Orchard Row is easily accessible by public transit and road. Lindmere central railway station is a ten-minute walk from the college, with regular bus connections stopping directly outside Orchard Row. For visitors traveling by car, visitor parking bays are available in our front courtyard, with additional street parking along Orchard Row.',
	'k63e6e59a' => 'College Instructors and Staff',
	'k6472a12a' => 'Daniel Brandt',
	'k6606e49d' => 'You will not be thrown into unpredictable situations alone. Throughout the thirty-two weeks, you will have regular mentoring, structured classroom sessions, and close tutor feedback, helping you transition smoothly from full-time schooling into a disciplined care environment.',
	'k666181ac' => 'January intake: 14 places left in Core Care',
	'k68069ce2' => 'Placement Coordinator',
	'k68a09e25' => 'Joining the college at nineteen gave me structure, discipline, and a clear sense of the work when my friends were unsure what to do, shares Joel Mensah. Joel entered the Core Care Certificate directly after finishing school. Initially nervous about assisting older adults with personal hygiene, Joel found that the step-by-step drills and volunteer scenarios removed his apprehension before placement began.',
	'k68e33662' => 'The longer read: inside the practice room.',
	'k69b4f023' => 'The kit had changed. So had I.',
	'k69db7612' => 'How are mentors chosen and supported?',
	'k69fcf35b' => 'About Mimamori College',
	'k6a552905' => 'Mimamori College is located at 18 Orchard Row, Lindmere. For general enquiries, course questions, or admissions guidance, you can call our main telephone line at +1 555 0142. If you prefer to reach us electronically, email our admissions desk directly at hello@mimamoricollege.example.',
	'k6adf97f8' => 'None',
	'k6b53cf06' => '32 weeks full-time',
	'k6bbaf775' => 'Prospective applicants, career changers, and family members are invited to our next campus open morning on Saturday 21 November at 10:00. Held at 18 Orchard Row in Lindmere, this event provides an informal opportunity to explore our practice room, view clinical hoisting equipment, and speak with instructors. Principal Ingrid Halvorsen and Lead Instructor Rosa Delgado will be present to explain our 32-week curriculum and answer questions about clinical placements.',
	'k6cd892b4' => 'Practical placement is the cornerstone of our training model. Students complete 420 hours of hands-on experience across twenty-two partner care homes, supervised by named workplace mentors.',
	'k6f1e2f9a' => 'Three stages',
	'k7040d3da' => 'Leaving school',
	'k71034b2e' => 'Hosting a student is free. One named mentor, two days a week.',
	'k718a2626' => 'Mei-Lin Tsai',
	'k72077835' => 'Over the term break, Director of Practice Samuel Adeyemi and Clinical Skills Nurse Tomasz Nowak conducted a full inspection and recalibration of all clinical training apparatus in our Lindmere skills room. New slide sheets, transfer boards, and mobile hoist batteries have been installed across all four profiling bed bays. These regular audits ensure that every student practices with modern, dependable equipment that strictly matches current residential care standards. Regular practice room hours remain 08:45 to 15:30 daily, maintaining our strict one-to-eight supervision ratio during practical laboratory drills.',
	'k72e69f1e' => 'Tomasz Nowak is our Clinical Skills Nurse, offering twelve years of acute nursing and residential care experience. Tomasz oversees clinical hygiene, medication documentation principles, vital signs recording, and basic skin integrity management. In the practice room, Tomasz demonstrates clinical observation techniques, teaching trainees how to recognize early signs of physical deterioration or dehydration in older adults. His calm, methodical teaching style helps learners overcome anxieties regarding clinical procedures, ensuring they understand both the practical execution and the physiological reasons behind each daily care task.',
	'k7361976b' => 'Director of Practice',
	'k747c30a6' => 'Bursary applications for new applicants',
	'k75c63d7b' => 'The Evening Route delivers the exact same curriculum and qualification as our full-time certificate over 48 weeks. Classes meet on Monday and Wednesday evenings from 18:00 to 21:00, alongside mandatory practical sessions on Saturdays. This route is ideal for learners who must maintain employment or family commitments while training. It includes the complete 420 hours of placement coordinated through partner care homes.',
	'k76feb545' => 'Weeks 1–8',
	'k7711ba84' => 'If you have worked in care previously but stepped away for family commitments or other work, the sector may have changed since you left. Moving techniques, documentation standards, and equipment models evolve regularly. Our Return to Care course runs for six weeks on a part-time schedule, allowing you to update your physical skills, review modern hoisting guidelines, and re-establish your professional confidence.',
	'k775a9a8d' => '48 weeks, Monday and Wednesday evenings and Saturdays. $7,200 plus $180 kit. Next start 12 January.',
	'k7aea8872' => 'Ingrid Halvorsen',
	'k7be5af2f' => 'Following your practical visit, we complete the reference check and review the clearance needed before a clinical placement. Once those checks are confirmed, Principal Ingrid Halvorsen issues a formal offer of admission. To accept your place, you return a signed enrolment agreement and arrange your tuition instalment plan or bursary documentation.',
	'k7c126529' => 'Mimamori College reminds prospective students that up to 6 bursaries, valued at $1,500 each, are available for the upcoming 12 January intake. These bursaries are designed to support dedicated candidates who demonstrate financial need. Bursary funds directly offset tuition fees for the Core Care Certificate or Evening Route.',
	'k7d91e95f' => 'Mei-Lin teaches person-centred communication, sensory adaptation, and behavioral understanding. Both instructors work directly beside students in our Lindmere practice room, demonstrating maneuvers step-by-step until each movement is performed safely and calmly.',
	'k7da84b75' => 'Samuel Adeyemi',
	'k7e29b0bb' => 'at eighteen allows you to step directly into a respected vocation. Working alongside experienced instructors and mature classmates, you will learn professional responsibility, emotional resilience, and the patient art of supporting someone’s daily life.',
	'k7ef24204' => 'Mon–Fri 08:30–17:30<br>Sat 09:00–12:00 in term',
	'k7f41e492' => 'Mimamori College maintains active partnerships with twenty-two local care providers across the region. Among our prominent partner homes is Larchfield House, where manager Greta Olsen has hosted our trainees for several years. We also place students at Mill Lane Care Home and The Orchards, both recognized for their calm environments and person-centred care routines.',
	'k8064f214' => 'Mimamori: to watch over, and to be watched over.',
