	'k8c1df93c' => 'Practice room, classroom, placement',
	'k8c265388' => 'Getting here',
	'k8c85eb51' => 'A named mentor, two days a week, and a college tutor visit every fortnight.',
	'k8ca68c5d' => 'Our training environment is supportive, but we cannot waive attendance requirements or safety assessments. Taking time to stabilize personal commitments or physical health will ensure you gain the full benefit of our intensive curriculum when you are ready.',
	'k8d2339f9' => 'Lunch, forty-five minutes',
	'k8dc04952' => 'Eight units taught in short seminars between practice sessions.',
	'k8deba755' => 'Academic direction',
	'k8e108af3' => 'Aisha Rahman is our Placement Coordinator, drawing on ten years of care sector networking to oversee our relationships with twenty-two partner homes. Aisha matches students to appropriate hosts like Larchfield House and monitors student progress on placement shifts. Daniel Brandt leads Learner Support, bringing nine years of experience in adult educational mentoring.',
	'k8f6c281e' => 'In our skills laboratory, we enforce a strict ratio of one instructor to eight students. We avoid large lecture theaters and automated grading, ensuring that every learner receives individual mentoring, daily performance reviews, and personal feedback throughout their study.',
	'k9029899a' => 'How a home takes a student on placement',
	'k902cb76e' => 'Applicants who have completed their initial application form are encouraged to schedule their practical visit and interview promptly. Bursary applications for this intake must be submitted no later than four weeks prior to the start date. For assistance with your application, contact hello@mimamoricollege.example.',
	'k90b52b30' => 'Saturday 21 November at 10:00. No need to book.',
	'k91381088' => 'The mentor works directly beside the student on every shift, observing transfers, reviewing daily notes, and modeling compassionate care. Mentors do not replace college instructors; instead, they provide steady, real-time guidance as students learn to adapt laboratory techniques to the realities of residential life.',
	'k9202bd5c' => 'Instalment Payment Options',
	'k921aa656' => 'At 11:00, the cohort gathers in the classroom for theoretical study. Tutors guide discussions on safeguarding legislation, infection prevention protocols, nutrition, and respectful record-keeping. We examine real-world case studies to help students understand the ethical responsibilities of daily care.',
	'k92e3efe7' => 'Step 1: Open Morning or Phone Enquiry',
	'k933e36e2' => 'During placement, you spend 420 supervised hours inside partner care homes. This balanced approach ensures that every theoretical concept studied in the morning is tested practically in our clinical lab and applied responsibly in actual residential care settings.',
	'k9405c3af' => 'Route',
	'k94511553' => 'Young adults aged eighteen and above can join the Core Care Certificate directly after leaving school. Care work is demanding and requires emotional maturity, but starting early allows you to build foundational technical skills that last an entire career. We teach you how to listen carefully, maintain clear professional boundaries, and work effectively alongside registered nurses and experienced senior carers.',
	'k95f681a7' => 'Your application begins with an informal visit or phone call. We encourage all prospective students to attend our free open morning on Saturday 21 November at 10:00, where you can tour the practice room, meet tutors, and ask questions. There is no need to pre-book your attendance for open mornings.',
	'k9621528d' => 'Read student stories',
	'k9639e32c' => 'Apply',
	'k96598787' => 'See the courses',
	'k9680417c' => 'A six-week part-time refresher after time away.',
	'k981cb035' => 'Changing career from any first job',
	'k9879b52c' => 'If you represent a care home and are interested in hosting students on placement, we welcome your enquiry. Hosting our trainees is entirely free for partner homes. Placement Coordinator Aisha Rahman can arrange a visit to discuss placement arrangements, mentor orientation, and student schedules.',
	'k98f2cf35' => 'January intake',
	'k98f5e8e5' => 'The Core Care Certificate',
	'k9a5c9cd7' => 'Assessment Methods and Competency Sign-Off',
	'k9a6eeae3' => 'College Address and Contact Details',
	'k9b03aef5' => 'Return to Care',
	'k9d85f907' => 'Who the year is for',
	'k9db79c5e' => 'Practical curriculum',
	'k9ed1c9f8' => 'After the first eight weeks, three college days and two placement days a week.',
	'k9fa72f8a' => '© 2009–2026 Mimamori College. A fictional college: its people, homes, courses and fees are samples.',
	'ka0b29f63' => 'We examine your commitment to punctual attendance from 08:45 each morning, your willingness to work collaboratively in small teams, and your capacity to communicate with patience and respect. These practical qualities form the true foundation of dependable care work.',
	'ka0c0aed2' => 'Four steps from enquiry to an offer, with no application fee.',
	'ka224d19e' => '“The first time I supported someone from a wheelchair to a bed, my instructor’s hand was right on my arm. That quiet steadiness stays with you when you enter a resident’s home.”',
	'ka334e7eb' => '28 September',
	'ka488e9a8' => '420 hours with a named mentor in one of twenty-two partner homes.',
	'ka4909e7b' => 'Core Care Certificate',
	'ka4f79195' => 'What went well and what to redo, day ends 15:30.',
	'ka4f9307a' => 'Step 2: Apply',
	'ka4ffdcf0' => 'Top',
	'ka6d7b8c9' => 'Safe Moving and Handling is an intensive two-day practical workshop led by Rosa Delgado. Designed to teach injury prevention, spinal mechanics, and equipment operation, the course takes place entirely within our Lindmere practice room. Students learn the safe operation of slide sheets, standing aids, ceiling track hoists, and mobile hoists under strict tutor supervision.',
	'ka76d4ef5' => 'Time',
	'ka795976f' => 'Dementia Care Certificate',
	'ka7c63141' => 'Leaving school to start at 18',
	'ka96067a6' => 'Partner homes',
	'kab92935f' => '10 weeks, one evening a week',
	'kac170391' => 'Start the Core Care Certificate at 18.',
	'kacf99c76' => 'Getting to 18 Orchard Row',
	'kad157e4f' => 'Host Home Commitments and Standards',
	'kadd45aa1' => 'Open day',
	'kae13e51f' => 'Placement',
	'kaf23f148' => 'Compare all five courses',
	'kb0c4019c' => 'Meet the instructors',
	'kb11682d3' => 'Thirty-two weeks full-time: eight units, 420 hours on placement, and a practice-room day that starts at 08:45.',
	'kb22590c7' => 'Care work requires physical stamina, steady emotional balance, and reliable punctuality. If you are currently dealing with severe unresolved physical back injuries, chronic unmanaged exhaustion, or personal circumstances that prevent you from attending scheduled shifts reliably, we recommend waiting twelve months before applying. The course involves regular bending, transfer maneuvers, and early morning starts from 08:45.',
	'kb311a3fe' => 'Morning',
	'kb3fa5c10' => 'How the College Is Run',
	'kb5131ba5' => 'If you cannot attend in person, you can call our admissions office at +1 555 0142 between 08:30 and 17:30 Monday through Friday. Our team will answer questions regarding schedules, fees, and accommodation, helping you choose the best study route for your circumstances.',
	'kb5134198' => 'We believe in transparent, straightforward pricing with no hidden registration costs or examination fees. Below are the complete fees for all courses offered at Mimamori College.',
	'kb60c3454' => '32 weeks full-time. $6,800 plus $180 kit. Next start 12 January.',
	'kb6de8682' => 'Mimamori College was established in 2009 to provide thorough, ethical, and unhurried caregiver training for adult learners. Based at 18 Orchard Row in Lindmere, we are an independent vocational institution focused exclusively on foundational care skills.',
	'kb9ad88a7' => 'Working under a strict ratio of one instructor to eight trainees, you practice assisting individuals from wheelchairs to beds, applying slide sheets, and positioning pillows to prevent pressure injuries. Instructors correct posture, hand placement, and verbal communication in real time.',
	'kba2a9c6c' => 'Length',
	'kba469266' => 'Transfers and mobility drills with one instructor to eight students.',
	'kba59a7a0' => 'Intakes are strictly capped at twenty-four students to preserve our 1:8 ratio in the practice room. When an intake is full, a qualified applicant may be offered a place in the following cohort, which begins on 7 September.',
	'kba81ce2a' => 'Step 2: Submitting Your Application',
	'kbb053118' => 'Study support and bursaries',
	'kbbbabdbe' => 'Role',
	'kbbfe8b16' => 'From retail, hospitality, offices or trades. No care experience needed.',
	'kbcc254b5' => 'Phone',
	'kbd20ca87' => 'Teaches',
	'kbe02e91e' => 'Independent Vocational Standards',
	'kbe9ddf1e' => 'Practice room time, seminars and instructor feedback.',
	'kbf8a710f' => 'Placement is supervised practice, not cover for a short-staffed floor.',
	'kbfce73ad' => 'Tuition is $320, which includes a college record of the two days once the standard transfer practice is completed. This course is ideal for personal assistants, community support staff, or family caregivers who need immediate, practical instruction in moving individuals with dignity and safety.',
	'kbfe72f18' => 'How to Apply',
	'kc0463b72' => 'The training day begins promptly at 08:45 with morning handover in the classroom. Students review resident scenario logs, note changes in mobility or hydration, and prioritize daily care tasks just as professional teams do during shift changes. At 09:15, students transition to the practice room for two hours of focused physical training.',
	'kc2a35893' => 'For students',
	'kc2f2a428' => 'Instalments',
	'kc4080fb8' => 'Homes that host a student on placement',
	'kc539264c' => 'Mimamori College was founded in 2009 by educators and senior care clinicians who recognized a critical gap in vocational training. Many introductory courses relied heavily on short online modules, leaving trainees unprepared for the physical and emotional realities of bedside care. Our founders established a dedicated college built around simulated practice rooms, intensive instructor supervision, and long-term residential placements. Over seventeen years of continuous teaching, we have adhered to a simple standard: no student leaves the course until they can transfer, reposition, and support an older adult safely, confidently, and with genuine gentleness.',
	'kc5d36f5f' => 'Because class sizes are strictly capped at twenty-four students, you never queue for equipment. You spend your hours actively practicing, learning how to steady your own balance while ensuring the person you assist feels secure and respected.',
	'kc6bc9fe2' => 'Completing this college certificate does not confer statutory nurse registration or state licensing automatically. We encourage all prospective students to review the specific employment regulations in the region where they intend to practice, as our certificate serves as evidence of practical training rather than a government-issued license.',
	'kc6f6c5d6' => 'Four steps from enquiry to an offer.',
	'kc741a1ff' => 'Mimamori College prepares adult learners to enter care work with confidence, practical competence, and steady hands. Whether you are changing careers, refreshing past qualifications, or beginning your working life, our training is structured around direct practice and individual supervision.',
	'kc7702b26' => 'You will maintain a portfolio of daily reflective logs, supervisor observation reports, and completed placement timesheets. Before any student is permitted to support residents in a care home, Rosa Delgado and Tomasz Nowak must formally sign off their practical competency. This ensures that every graduate demonstrates safe, reliable, and compassionate physical care skills.',
	'kc771fbd7' => 'Equipment and materials',
	'kc7a4c39d' => 'To apply for a place at Mimamori College, you must be at least eighteen years old on your start date. We do not require previous care credentials, diplomas, or prior clinical experience. Every applicant must complete an identity check, provide two verifiable personal or professional references, and clear a standard criminal record check prior to placement.',
	'kc7e4e6d7' => 'The curriculum comprises eight ruled units designed to build comprehensive caregiver competence. Unit 1 covers the role of the carer and professional boundaries. Unit 2 addresses personal development and reflective practice. Unit 3 focuses on duty of care, legal responsibilities, and safeguarding adults. Unit 4 teaches effective communication and documentation.',
	'kc81398c2' => 'We offer five distinct training routes designed for different schedules and experience levels. Each course combines structured classroom study with supervised practical coaching in our Lindmere practice room.',
	'kc88ec12c' => 'Returning to care',
	'kc8c81328' => 'Attending an Open Morning',
	'kc9cabfcc' => 'Admissions are open for our upcoming full-time Core Care Certificate starting on 12 January. As of this week, exactly 14 places remain available in this cohort. Each intake is strictly limited to 24 students to preserve our 1:8 instructor ratio in the practice room.',
	'kca6be12d' => 'Uniform and kit',
	'kcb42a8ce' => 'Bursary Applications for New Applicants',
	'kcbd8944d' => 'Open morning',
	'kcc0ac792' => 'Tuition Fees and Kit Costs',
	'kccab2f82' => 'Open weekdays 08:30–17:30 and Saturday mornings 09:00–12:00 in term.',
	'kcd5ccc08' => 'The Core Care Certificate is our flagship thirty-two-week full-time qualification for career-changers and new entrants to care. Training takes place across our Lindmere skills laboratory, seminar rooms, and partner homes.',
	'kcdc54bd9' => 'January Intake: 14 Places Left in Core Care',
	'kce84c981' => 'Open morning on Saturday 21 November at 10:00. No need to book.',
	'kceacec77' => 'Fees, Bursaries, and Financial Information',
	'kd0911503' => 'After twelve years managing customer accounts in retail banking, Noor joined our Core Care Certificate seeking work that felt genuinely personal. In the practice room, she learned how patient positioning and clear verbal cues ease physical transitions for older adults. Today, she works as a dedicated caregiver at Larchfield House, guiding new trainees with the same unhurried reassurance she received here.',
	'kd0fbda98' => 'Page not found',
	'kd12db4cd' => 'Bicycle storage is located beside the main entrance. When arriving, please sign in at the reception desk in our main building, where our staff will welcome you and provide visitor passes.',
	'kd189f954' => 'Our Partner Care Homes',
	'kd1a9a1e1' => 'How to apply',
	'kd254861f' => 'Notices',
	'kd2a7eb63' => 'Request a prospectus',
	'kd2b24b38' => 'The Core Care Certificate divides its 32 weeks into three distinct learning environments. In the practice room, you work in small groups of eight with dedicated instructors, rehearsing transfers, bed positioning, and personal hygiene techniques. In the classroom, you study infection control principles, ethical duty of care, safeguarding, and communication skills.',
	'kd3df3f47' => 'To apply, you must first complete your practical assessment day and hold an offer of admission. All completed bursary forms and supporting financial documentation must be submitted to Daniel Brandt in Learner Support at least four weeks before term begins.',
	'kd3f7b656' => 'Three Placement Stages',
	'kd49ef787' => '18 Orchard Row, Lindmere<br>+1 555 0142<br>hello@mimamoricollege.example',
	'kd4dd1a42' => 'At fifty-two, leaving warehouse logistics felt like a gamble, but the college taught me that my life experience was an asset, says Peter Vance. Peter joined the full-time program with concerns about returning to a structured learning environment after thirty years. However, our small cohorts and practical focus suited his hands-on background.',
	'kd4e6546a' => 'The college does not state a job, a wage, a pass rate, or a government licence as the result of any course. We teach real, grounded care fundamentals. Our curriculum is developed in consultation with our twenty-two partner care homes, so the skills rehearsed in our Lindmere practice room reflect current clinical equipment and daily home routines.',
	'kd5210e24' => 'Handover practice and review of overnight resident reports.',
	'kd5ba887e' => 'The Dementia Care Certificate is a specialized ten-week program delivered one evening per week. Led by Mei-Lin Tsai, this course focuses on person-centred communication, environmental adaptation, distress response, and supporting families through progressive memory loss. Trainees examine real-life scenarios, practice non-verbal de-escalation methods, and explore ways to preserve personal dignity in residential living.',
	'kd61ac03a' => 'What is included',
	'kd73508ed' => 'As our current cohort prepares for clinical placements, Mimamori College extends its appreciation to our 22 partner care homes across the Lindmere region. Trainees in Weeks 9 through 28 will begin their two-day weekly placement shifts alongside their named workplace mentors. We thank homes such as Larchfield House, managed by Greta Olsen, Mill Lane Care Home, and The Orchards for providing supervised, supernumerary learning environments. Placement Coordinator Aisha Rahman will conduct regular weekly visits to host facilities to support both students and mentors throughout the term.',
	'kd74abae3' => 'Eight weeks first, then every college day. One instructor to eight students.',
	'kd751e648' => 'Noor Haddad: Former Bank Teller',
	'kd7888459' => 'Five routes, from a two-day workshop to the 32-week certificate.',
	'kd7bfdeb8' => 'Samuel oversees all practical standards, designs realistic scenario assessments, and directly supervises our instructor team. Together, they ensure that every policy, lesson plan, and clinical assessment reflects the highest ethical standards of modern compassionate care.',
	'kd80954e8' => 'Step 4: References and Formal Offer',
	'kda419f07' => 'Most of our students come from outside the care sector, arriving from retail, hospitality, office administration, or manual trades. You do not need previous healthcare experience to begin the Core Care Certificate. What matters is patience, attentiveness, and the willingness to learn physical routines in a methodical way.',
	'kdb5eb841' => 'Support',
	'kdbda66b3' => 'Moving and handling',
	'kdd1ba187' => 'News',
	'kdd3edae6' => 'Why the name Mimamori?',
	'kdd7bf230' => 'Address',
	'kdd99ade1' => '6 weeks part-time',
	'kddd1cd24' => 'Open Morning: Saturday 21 November at 10:00',
	'ke065465b' => 'Placement Enquiries for Care Homes',
	'ke0aa7dad' => 'Ingrid Halvorsen and Samuel Adeyemi',
	'ke0c45e31' => 'One story from last year',
	'ke150278e' => 'Who it’s for',
	'ke1575716' => 'The eight units',
	'ke1ad4563' => 'With close guidance from Rosa Delgado and daily drills in bed transfers, Noor built physical confidence step-by-step. During placement at Larchfield House, Noor discovered the value of unhurried conversation during morning routines. That morning pace is what Noor still describes: time enough to sit with someone and not hurry the task.',
	'ke1da0abf' => '+1 555 0142, Monday to Friday 08:30 to 17:30.',
	'ke1f30c4e' => 'Step 4: Offer',
	'ke2f73ccc' => 'Morning Handover and Practice Room',
	'ke38ca4b9' => 'Student stories',
	'ke3b249fc' => 'Come and see the practice room',
	'ke3cf53b8' => 'Evening Route Admissions for 12 January',
	'ke512dc46' => 'Applications for bursaries must be submitted four weeks prior to the intake start date. Decisions are determined by a faculty committee led by Principal Ingrid Halvorsen based on financial need and personal commitment.',
	'ke519bc35' => 'Every weekday begins promptly at 08:45 and concludes at 15:30, structured to reflect the disciplined rhythm of professional residential care. Students learn through direct physical practice rather than prolonged lecture hours.',
	'ke55df28f' => 'Practicing in the Lindmere skills lab restored her professional confidence without the need to repeat a multi-month diploma. Camille appreciated the supportive, non-judgmental feedback from instructors Tomasz Nowak and Rosa Delgado, who treated her past background with dignity while updating her technique.',
	'ke576be7c' => 'Daniel assists trainees with study skills, time management, and any personal hurdles that arise during the thirty-two weeks. Both Aisha and Daniel ensure that no student struggles in isolation throughout their time at Mimamori College.',
	'ke64d5684' => 'Open morning on Saturday 21 November at 10:00.',
	'ke69af091' => 'We welcome prospective students, families, and care home managers to visit our Lindmere campus. Contact our admissions team by phone, email, or visit during our scheduled office hours.',
	'ke727d664' => 'weeks, full-time on the Core Care Certificate',
	'ke7625c28' => 'Two days with slide sheets, transfer belts and a ceiling hoist, practised until your back and hands know them.',
	'ke772b7f0' => 'I was nineteen and the oldest person in the room was ninety-one.',
	'ke78d2399' => 'Our practice room at 18 Orchard Row is equipped to replicate a modern care facility. It contains four adjustable profiling beds, modern mobile hoists, ceiling track systems, wheelchairs, and private wash areas. Stocked with transfer boards, slide sheets, and standard clinical charts, the space allows students to master equipment in a calm, controlled setting.',
	'ke7c32000' => 'Aisha Rahman places every student with a named mentor.',
	'ke868507e' => 'About the college',
	'ke92c8925' => 'Lead Instructor',
	'ke94e1bc2' => 'Clinical skills',
	'ke96d3703' => 'Tomasz Nowak',
	'ke9fcae82' => 'Open morning confirmed for Saturday 21 November at 10:00.',
	'keacef9f4' => 'Practice Room, Classroom, and Placement',
	'keade3927' => 'Who It Is For',
	'keb7297e9' => 'Fee',
	'kec39832b' => 'The Eight Core Units',
	'kec432e31' => 'One published price per route, instalments and six bursaries.',
	'ked8968b4' => 'Noor Haddad',
	'kee0dae97' => 'hours on placement with one host home and a named mentor',
	'kef0bb29c' => 'Aisha Rahman',
	'kef276337' => 'Practice room equipment, learning materials and assessment.',
	'kefe45a6d' => 'Tuition and teaching',
	'kf008458d' => 'Students have full access to college library resources, practice hoists, and clinical simulation models. There are no additional fees for retaking practical competency checks, re-sitting scenario assessments, or receiving one-on-one learner support from Daniel Brandt.',
	'kf0712ca0' => 'Midday',
	'kf0910df7' => '12 January: 14 places left in the Core Care Certificate',
	'kf0d06c40' => 'Visit us at 18 Orchard Row, Lindmere, to see our equipment and speak with instructors.',
	'kf2e93660' => 'We currently partner with twenty-two homes across the region, including Larchfield House, Mill Lane Care Home, and The Orchards. Contact Aisha directly by calling +1 555 0142 or emailing hello@mimamoricollege.example with the subject line Partner Placement Enquiry to arrange a meeting.',
	'kf337e6e4' => 'One evening a week for ten weeks on talking with, and supporting, a person living with dementia.',
	'kf3ed24d6' => '48 weeks, evenings and Saturdays',
	'kf4e7699b' => 'Tuition is $7,200, payable in four interest-free instalments across your study terms, with an additional $180 kit fee. This pathway is specifically designed for learners maintaining weekday jobs while training. Contact our admissions team at +1 555 0142 for detailed timetables.',
	'kf4f63e65' => 'Weeks 9–28',
	'kf5c2ab8b' => 'Step 1: Enquire',
	'kf66df6f3' => 'Assessment at Mimamori College is continuous, practical, and grounded in direct observation. You will not sit stressful written examinations. Instead, instructors evaluate your technique during simulated care routines, assessing your manual handling, hand hygiene, and respectful communication.',
	'kf69dbbab' => 'Our admissions process is designed to help you decide whether care training is the right fit for your temperament and goals. We evaluate every applicant through conversation, practical observation, and personal references.',
	'kf7830d49' => 'Partner homes make a clear commitment to student welfare and educational safety. Hosting a student is entirely free for the home; no fees are charged or paid. Host homes agree to provide a safe, welcoming learning environment, assign a dedicated named mentor for every scheduled shift, and release students for college training days.',
	'kf7a778bf' => 'All notices',
	'kf80391c5' => 'Students are not asked to work unassisted or to carry out procedures beyond the competencies already signed off in the practice room. In return, host homes welcome trainees who have rehearsed infection control, moving mechanics, and respectful communication before their first day on placement.',
	'kf806edac' => 'Classroom Seminars and Midday Break',
	'kf8690d35' => 'Every student is matched with one named mentor at their host home. Mentors are senior care workers selected for their patience, clear communication, and adherence to dignified care practices. Before hosting, mentors meet with Director of Practice Samuel Adeyemi and Placement Coordinator Aisha Rahman to align on learning objectives.',
	'kf900b59b' => 'Saturday 21 November, 10:00, no need to book',
	'kf94d0616' => 'Because we are focused exclusively on care education, our resources go to modern hoists, profiling beds, infection control supplies, and high instructor staffing levels. This independence lets us keep the training patient and unhurried, day after day.',
	'kf9604eed' => 'The word mimamori is a Japanese concept that translates to watching over or caring with watchful eyes. It describes an approach to care where a caregiver remains attentive, protective, and present without being intrusive or restrictive. In traditional caregiving, mimamori means observing subtle changes in posture, breathing, mood, or hydration, allowing an individual to retain independence while knowing help is beside them. We adopted this name because it perfectly embodies the philosophy we teach our trainees: care is not something done to a person, but a steady presence maintained alongside them.',
	'kf972c324' => 'College Notices and Announcements',
	'kf9b16a35' => 'Inside the Lindmere Practice Room',
	'kfc07c21e' => 'Welcoming our 22 placement partner homes',
	'kfc0a75e0' => 'Courses and Training Pathways',
	'kfcf389d6' => 'Each partner home signs an agreement ensuring students are treated as supernumerary learners rather than replacement staff. Students rotate through these reputable homes to experience diverse care environments, from residential dementia units to specialized assisted living wings.',
	'kfd1f9030' => 'Five routes, one practice room.',
	'kfd4a5812' => 'The remaining three payments are scheduled at regular intervals across your study terms. We charge no administration fees, interest, or late penalties for using this payment plan, ensuring that financial schedules remain predictable and manageable throughout your training.',
	'kfd4d9996' => 'You will also write a brief statement explaining why you wish to train in care and how you plan to manage the course schedule. Applications for our upcoming intake on 12 January are currently being reviewed, with only 14 places remaining. Early submission leaves time to complete the practical visit and the reference check.',
	'kfde68a3d' => 'Learner support with Daniel Brandt, before and during the course.',
	'kfec9f3aa' => 'Morning handover in the classroom',
	'kff98676e' => 'A training day',
	'kfff3e55e' => 'Admissions',
